      "value": "@{5a9b3ad0f5e0532e3ea468be|full_name}\n\nIt’s not aggressive it’s a perfect speed and height as is. Even in public worlds I haven’t seen that many people using it to the point it could be considered anything even approaching a nuisance. \n\nSo what if they have to disable props? It’s not that big of a deal. Prop aren’t even used that much to begin with, so it’s not really a huge sacrifice to turn them off if necessary. \n\nJust because VRC seems intent on something doesn’t mean it’s a rigid rule set in stone. I’d say the broom should be an exception and treated like a quality of life improvement.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
